WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
Two lamps stand far apart on open ground.

2
00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:05.390
Both flash once.

3
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:07.910
You stand still, and
your measurements say:

4
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.180
same moment, exactly.

5
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:14.440
Now a spacecraft streaks
past at a high, steady speed.

6
00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.190
Its crew times the same two flashes.

7
00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.240
Could they honestly disagree about
whether the flashes happened together?

8
00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:24.140
In this mission, you'll
draw space–time diagrams,

9
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.000
where every object traces a world line.

10
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:30.690
Then you'll meet one quantity that
every observer measures the same,

11
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.180
however they move.

12
00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:36.010
Your mission: decide whether
the crew can honestly disagree,

13
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.530
and show why on a space–time diagram.
